AtomEngine @VERSION@ - source SDK
=================================

A C++20 game engine on SDL3's GPU API (Direct3D 12), as source: the
engine, its framework, the development tools (Atom Workspace,
AtomProjectTool, AtomLevelCheck), the shared content, the pinned
dependencies and HelloAtom, the smallest app. Licence: MIT (LICENSE.txt);
each dependency keeps its own (external/*/, Engine/Debug/Fonts/,
Content/Fonts/).

Requirements: Windows 10/11, Visual Studio 2022 or later (C++20), CMake
3.26+, and dxc (the Windows SDK or the Vulkan SDK) for the shaders.

1. Build the engine and its tools

    cmake -B build -S .
    cmake --build build --config Release
    build\bin\Release\AtomWorkspace\AtomWorkspace.exe

2. Make a game - anywhere, its own folder and build

    In the workspace: File > Create Project. Or:
    build\bin\Release\AtomProjectTool.exe create --in <folder> --name MyGame

    MyGame\ has its own CMakeLists.txt that adds this engine below it.
    Add Source\Main.cpp (start from Apps\Samples\HelloAtom\Main.cpp), then:

    cd <folder>\MyGame
    cmake --preset atom
    cmake --build build --config Debug

    or press Build and Run in the workspace.

docs\Getting-Started.md walks through both; docs\Architecture.md explains
how the engine is put together. Not included: the bundled games and the
Showcase, the Blender content build and its .blend sources, the
engine's own tests and development scripts.
